48325b0ba4c973d076a2273712b747715179a065:
### How many email accounts do I need? {slug: cold-email-agent/faq/email-accounts/how-many-email-accounts-do-i-need}
Get here: In the left sidebar, click "Email accounts"
Each account sends 30 campaign emails/day by default (changeable per inbox; 30 to 40 is the safe range). 300/day needs about 10 accounts; 100/day about 4. Start with at least 3 per campaign.

1b10c8e3825f8e464812b29623ac157bc02b29c1:
### How much do inboxes cost? {slug: cold-email-agent/faq/email-accounts/how-much-do-inboxes-cost}
Get here: In the left sidebar, click "Email accounts"
Domains are billed yearly, inboxes monthly. Exact prices show at checkout. Subscriptions renew on the 15th of each month. Inbox purchases are not refundable.

dd7c323a5b49f7455d85b30dacb60b0e6c0f1e82:
### What are pre-warmed inboxes? {slug: cold-email-agent/faq/email-accounts/what-are-pre-warmed-inboxes}
Get here: In the left sidebar, click "Email accounts", then "Add inboxes"
Accounts that sent and received warm-up emails for 4+ weeks before purchase, so providers recognise them and spam is less likely. Each domain has a set number of inboxes, shown when you pick it. SPF, DKIM, DMARC are preconfigured.

859c8b3f6da40bb238574b5568c34ee855c3a1df:
### What does the health score mean? {slug: cold-email-agent/faq/email-accounts/what-does-the-health-score-mean}
Get here: In the left sidebar, click "Email accounts"
Shown in "Warm-up health". It measures whether warm-up emails land in inboxes, not real campaign deliverability. 90%+ is ready to send; below 90% give more warm-up time before campaigns.

e47aad978eb3bbf739c8ac5cd5e2db95b1ffa8bc:
### What is the warmup period? {slug: cold-email-agent/faq/email-accounts/what-is-the-warmup-period}
Get here: In the left sidebar, click "Email accounts"
Warm-up builds sending reputation by exchanging emails in a warm-up network. Pre-warmed inboxes skip it; DFY accounts need about 2 weeks; those still warming show "Warming up".

